Q: User input Form alignment A: <p>There are two methods of fixing this problem.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Using Grid instead of LabeledContent</p>
<p>It allows you to align items in columns across multiple rows automatically.</p>
</li>
<li><p>If you want to keep LabeledContent, You should follow this code.</p>
<pre><code>Section {
    VStack(alignment: .leading) {
        LabeledContent(&quot;Search Value:&quot;) { ... }
        LabeledContent(&quot;Tolerance:&quot;) { ... }
    }
    .frame(maxWidth: 300) // Constrain the stack, not the individual items
}
</code></pre>
</li>
</ol>

Q: Foreach not accumulating data in result variable as intended A: <p>Use below code, In your case $sidebar value always override </p>

<pre><code>$authority = getWithResult('authorites', 'UserId', $id);
$sidebar = [];
foreach($authority as $yetki){
    $sidebar[] = getWithResult('sidebar', 'Id', $yetki-&gt;SidebarId);
}
print_r($sidebar);
</code></pre>

